Package: hd-kernel
Version: @META_DEB_VERSION@
Architecture: amd64
Maintainer: Erik Van Hamme <erik.vanhamme@gmail.com>
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Depends: linux-image-@RELEASE@ (= @KERNEL_DEB_VERSION@),
 zfs-modules-@RELEASE@ (= @ZFS_DEB_VERSION@)
Conflicts: linux-image-amd64, linux-headers-amd64, linux-base-amd64
Section: kernel
Priority: optional
Description: HyprDebian kernel with a prebuilt ZFS module
 Depends on the most recent HyprDebian kernel of @SUITE@ and its ZFS module,
 so that they are installed and upgraded with it. The kernel is the kernel of
 Debian, linux @KERNEL_VERSION@, with its patches and its config; the ZFS
 module is that of zfs-linux @ZFS_VERSION@, built against it. Both are built
 on the build server and signed with a key that is made for the build and
 thrown away, so a system needs neither DKMS nor a compiler for ZFS, and
 the kernel trusts no other key for its modules.
 .
 It replaces the kernel of Debian: installing it removes linux-image-amd64,
 linux-headers-amd64 and linux-base-amd64. See hd-kernel(7).
